            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The case of a woman with anomalous origin of the circumflex coronary artery that communicates with the left ventricle via a fistula, revealed by typical angina, is described and the several pathomechanisms involved are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
